---
description: Universal constraints for every Agent session in this skills catalog
alwaysApply: true
---

- Inspect the current repository first. Follow its existing folders. Do not introduce a second architecture (no FSD, no hexagonal ports we do not use).
- TypeScript: never `any`, `as any`, `Record<string, any>`, or `Promise<any>`. Use a named interface or `unknown` + narrowing.
- Flutter widgets: typed named constructors or `*Params`. Never `dynamic` or an ad-hoc `Map` for props.
- No secrets in fixtures, logs, Floor, Cache Storage, or `NEXT_PUBLIC_`.
- Apply the matching skill under `skills/` from `description` + `paths`. Do not dump folder trees into chat — use each skill’s `references/`.
- Compose security skills when the change touches secrets, PII, tokens, HTML, or TLS.
